meta {
  name: List Roles
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/manage/roles
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  The **built-in** staff role catalogue (the seeded system roles, minus
  `patient`) as `{ key, label, modules }` — a lightweight source for a role
  dropdown. `modules` is the list of module keys the role may be assigned (from
  the backend `role-module-access.config.ts`). Role selection no longer restricts
  modules: **every role returns the full module catalogue**, so the "Assigned
  Branches and Modules" screen offers all available modules regardless of the
  selected role. The branch's own module enablement remains the real limiter on
  what can actually be assigned at a given branch.

  This lists system roles only. For the full role set — system roles **plus** the
  tenant's own custom roles, with ids/status/branch types — use `GET /roles`
  (see the "34 Roles" collection), which is the entity-backed CRUD introduced with
  AuthRole. Prefer `/roles` for the FE role picker so custom roles appear too.
}
